ruggle: Struggle deals damage to target creature equal to the number of lands you control.\n//\nSurvive: Aftermath (Cast this spell only from your graveyard. Then exile it.)\nEach player shuffles their graveyard into their library.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-04-21","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant // Sorcery"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}","name":"Thran Foundry","oracle_id":"88079144-8d8e-4f98-9bee-3762540c94ca","oracle_text":"{1}, {T}, Exile this artifact: Target player shuffles their graveyard into their library.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"1999-06-07","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"A spell with aftermath cast from a graveyard will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, it's countered, or it leaves the stack in some other way.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"All split cards have two card faces on a single card, and you put a split card onto the stack with only the half you're casting. The characteristics of the half of the card you didn't cast are ignored while the spell is on the stack. For example, if an effect prevents you from casting green spells, you can cast Destined of Destined // Lead, but not Lead.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each split card has two names. If an effect instructs you to choose a card name, you may choose one, but not both.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each split card is a single card. For example, if you discard one, you've discarded one card, not two. If an effect counts the number of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard, Destined // Lead counts once, not twice.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another effect allows you to cast a split card with aftermath from a graveyard, you may cast either half. If you cast the half that has aftermath, you'll exile the card if it would leave the stack.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another effect allows you to cast a split card with aftermath from any zone other than a graveyard, you can't cast the half with aftermath.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast the first half of a split card with aftermath during your turn, you'll have priority immediately after it resolves. You can cast the half with aftermath from your graveyard before any player can take any other action if it's legal for you to do so.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Split cards with aftermath have a new frame treatment\u2014the half you can cast from your hand is oriented the same as other cards you'd cast from your hand, while the half you can cast from your graveyard is a traditional split card half. This frame treatment is for your convenience and has no rules significance.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While not on the stack, the characteristics of a split card are the combination of its two halves. For example, Destined // Lead is a green and black card, it is both an instant card and a sorcery card, and its mana value is 6. This means that if an effect allows you to cast a card with mana value 2 from your hand, you can't cast Destined. This is a change from the previous rules for split cards.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-04-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a player has no cards in their graveyard when Survive resolves, that player just shuffles their library.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once you've started to cast a spell with aftermath from your graveyard, the card is immediately moved to the stack. Opponents can't try to stop the ability by exiling the card with an effect such as that of Crook of Condemnation.","oracle_id":"0b1f2522-960c-405f-9622-4cadbc7ba545","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Clear the Mind can target a player with no cards in their graveyard. That player shuffles their library and then you draw a card.","oracle_id":"141c33be-7a25-4981-b62c-efee8e8ec91d","published_at":"2019-01-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you choose yourself as the target for Clear the Mind, Clear the Mind will end up as the only card in your graveyard after it\u2019s done resolving.","oracle_id":"141c33be-7a25-4981-b62c-efee8e8ec91d","published_at":"2019-01-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the player\u2019s graveyard is empty, the player will shuffle their library, then you\u2019ll draw a card.","oracle_id":"260f95c5-4058-4627-981f-98b9eafc2265","published_at":"2014-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This card won't be put into your graveyard until after it's finished resolving, which means it won't be shuffled into your library as part of its own effect.","oracle_id":"296c4d2b-e41c-416b-807e-5b4db638ec57","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This card won\u2019t be put into your graveyard until after it\u2019s finished resolving, which means it won\u2019t be shuffled into your library as part of its own effect.","oracle_id":"6fe302f2-5594-478c-a66b-89b4b96e3611","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the player's graveyard is empty, the player will shuffle their library, then you'll draw a card.","oracle_id":"f325fd7a-dcae-4892-adf5-de9893a23ac5","published_at":"2015-02-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
